**Question:**
Write a program to check whether the entered PIN is correct or not. The correct PIN is **4321**. If the entered PIN matches 4321, display **"Correct PIN"**, otherwise display **"Incorrect PIN"**.

#**JAVA**
import java.util.Scanner;

public class pin{
    public static void main (String[] args){
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.println("Enter the PIN: ");
        int n = sc.nextInt();
        if(n==4321){
            System.out.println("This is the correct PIN.");
        }else{
            System.out.println("This is not the correct PIN.");
        }
    }
}

#**PYTHON**
n = int(input("Enter the value of PIN: "))

if n == 4321:
    print("Correct PIN")
else:
    print("Incorrect PIN")
